{"term":"commute","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9c9fabe7370db310f3","definition":"To exchange substantially; to abate but not abolish completely, a penalty, obligation, or payment in return for a great, single thing or an aggregate; to cash in; to lessen","example":"to commute tithes into rentcharges for a sum","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:48bb9385735d19422a","definition":"Of an operation, to be commutative, i.e. to have the property that changing the order of the operands does not change the result.","example":"A pair of matrices share the same set of eigenvectors if and only if they commute.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b11a53f36682dc2e90","definition":"A regular journey between two places, typically home and work.","example":"If you're hearing me then it means your ego has been commuted successfully into this CAT with zero errors. Only one warning by the way: it may take a moment to acclimatize to being a bodyless ego, but try not to worry too much.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f6aa627921003e899d","definition":"The route, time or distance of that journey.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:48e01690f4c94f922e","definition":"To regularly travel from one's home to one's workplace or school, or vice versa.","example":"I commute from Brooklyn to Manhattan by bicycle.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Canada, UK, US","register":"Canada, UK, US, intransitive","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted","commuter","counter-commute","postcommute","reverse-commute","reverse commute","telecommute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29315a59043e52bce3","definition":"To regularly travel from one place to another using public transport.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Philippines","register":"Philippines, intransitive","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted","commuter","counter-commute","postcommute","reverse-commute","reverse commute","telecommute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e464d7d46938d2078","definition":"To journey, to make a journey","example":"By one estimate, vultures either residing in or commuting into the Serengeti ecosystem during the annual migration—when 1.3 million white-bearded wildebeests shuffle between Kenya and Tanzania—historically consumed more meat than all mammalian carnivores in the Serengeti combined.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted","commuter","counter-commute","postcommute","reverse-commute","reverse commute","telecommute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/kəˈmjuːt/"},"wordFamily":["anticommute","commutability","commutable","commutant","commutation","commutative","commutive","uncommuted","commuter","counter-commute","postcommute","reverse-commute","reverse commute","telecommute"]}